issue_context.body:
**_Issue_**

When specifying a provider supplied signature algorithm in `SignatureAlgorithms` in `openssl.cnf`, the code point of this signature algorithm is not added to the `ClientHello`. Rather, the processing of the  `SignatureAlgorithms` list is stopped and all available signature algorithms (including all provider sigalgs) are added to the `ClientHello`. 

The equivalent for `Groups` in `openssl.cnf` is working correctly for provider supplied groups.

**_Root cause_**

The `tls1_set_sigalgs_list` [function](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/cf6342bc024868f5a55f2225f2e083415fb1329a/ssl/t1_lib.c#L2943) is [using](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/cf6342bc024868f5a55f2225f2e083415fb1329a/ssl/t1_lib.c#L2947C10-L2947C25) `CONF_parse_list` with `sig_cb` [callback function](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/cf6342bc024868f5a55f2225f2e083415fb1329a/ssl/t1_lib.c#L2874). The callback function limits the search for signature algorithms to the [content](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/cf6342bc024868f5a55f2225f2e083415fb1329a/ssl/t1_lib.c#L1375) of the sigalg_lookup_tbl and does not check any provider. 

**_Possible mitigation_**

By adding a code segment [here](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/cf6342bc024868f5a55f2225f2e083415fb1329a/ssl/t1_lib.c#L2899) to first check whether a provider would support a signature algorithm, the provider based signature algorithms can be correctly added to the `ClientHello`. 

A dummy, zeroized `SSL_CTX` is used which is initialized solely with the provider supplied signature algorithms using the [function](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/cf6342bc024868f5a55f2225f2e083415fb1329a/ssl/t1_lib.c#L707) `ssl_load_sigalgs`. Algorithm names and code points are then available from the `TLS_SIGALG_INFO` [structure](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/cf6342bc024868f5a55f2225f2e083415fb1329a/ssl/ssl_local.h#L772) which is [part of](https://github.com/openssl/openssl/blob/cf6342bc024868f5a55f2225f2e083415fb1329a/ssl/ssl_local.h#L1172) `SSL_CTX`.
```
    if (p == NULL) {
        /* We first check the providers */
        SSL_CTX *ctx_helper = OPENSSL_zalloc(sizeof(*ctx_helper));
        /* load provider sigalgs */
        if (!ctx_helper || !ssl_load_sigalgs(ctx_helper)) {
            ERR_raise(ERR_LIB_SSL, ERR_R_SSL_LIB);
            return 0;
        }
        /* Check if a provider supports the sigalg */
        for (int i=0; i < ctx_helper->sigalg_list_len; i++) {
            if (ctx_helper->sigalg_list[i].sigalg_name != NULL && strcmp(etmp, ctx_helper->sigalg_list[i].sigalg_name) == 0) {
                sarg->sigalgs[sarg->sigalgcnt++] = ctx_helper->sigalg_list[i].code_point;
                SSL_CTX_free(ctx_helper);
                return 1;
            }
        }
        SSL_CTX_free(ctx_helper);
        /* Check the built-in sigalgs */
        for (i = 0, s = sigalg_lookup_tbl; i < OSSL_NELEM(sigalg_lookup_tbl);
            ....
            ....
```

